{"id":"A2-L039","title":"Future: going to — production and review","cefr":"A2","level":"A2","unit":"A2-U03","focus":"Future — going to — produção e revisão","targets":{"grammar":"Future — going to — produção e revisão","pron":"gonna e wanna (reconhecimento)","verbs":["cost"],"pv":[],"expr":[],"words":["mile","quit","cost","expense","training plan","long run","pace","energy gel","blister","cramp","race bib","starting line","water station","recovery day","finish medal","shin"],"field":"Saúde cotidiana","genre":"Conto e trecho de peça","skill":"Fala","words_min":16},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 39 · Future: going to — production and review","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Future — going to — produção e revisão.","**Verbos:** cost.","**Pronúncia:** gonna e wanna (reconhecimento).","**16 palavras novas** (saúde cotidiana).","**Texto do dia:** conto e trecho de peça."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (A2):** eu consigo escrever um conto com planos e calcular quanto custa algo."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["Você começa a praticar tarefas curtas no formato das provas.","Esta aula treina **responder em frases completas (IELTS Speaking, TOEFL Speaking)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["mile","milha"],["quit","desistir"],["cost","custar"],["expense","despesa"],["training plan","plano de treino"],["long run","corrida longa"],["pace","ritmo"],["energy gel","gel de energia"],["blister","bolha"],["cramp","cãibra"],["race bib","número de corrida"],["starting line","linha de largada"],["water station","posto de água"],["recovery day","dia de recuperação"],["finish medal","medalha de chegada"],["shin","canela"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A short story","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"The Plan That Cost Too Much","paras":["Lia was going to run a marathon. She **bought** shoes that **cost** $200, a watch that **cost** $150 and a plan that **cost** $90 a month. “It **is going to cost** a lot,” said her mom.","Lia **was going to** quit, but her friend said, “Run with me.” It **cost** nothing. They **ran** the first mile in the park and **felt** great."],"kicker":"SHORT STORY","by":"A reader","gloss":[["marathon","maratona"],["quit","desistir"],["mile","milha"],["watch","relógio"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"Lia’s shoes cost $200.","ans":"T","why":"$200."},{"q":"The training with a friend cost $90.","ans":"F","why":"cost nothing."},{"q":"Lia ran the first mile.","ans":"T","why":"ran the first mile."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“marathon” = ?","opts":["maratona","corrida curta","gincana"],"ans":0,"why":"marathon."},{"q":"“quit” = ?","opts":["desistir","continuar","começar"],"ans":0,"why":"quit."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"going to: past and future","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Forma","Exemplo"],"rows":[["plano agora","**I am going to run.**"],["plano que mudou","**I was going to quit.**"],["pergunta de preço","**How much does it cost?**"]],"cap":"going to: past and future"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"**cost** é irregular: **cost – cost – cost**."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"I ___ to run a marathon. (be going, past)","a":"was going","why":"plano passado."},{"s":"The shoes ___ $200. (cost, past)","a":"cost","why":"cost-cost."},{"s":"It ___ to cost a lot. (be going)","a":"is going","why":"previsão."},{"s":"How much ___ it cost? (do)","a":"does","why":"does."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["marathon","maratona"],["mile","milha"],["quit","desistir"],["cost","custar"],["expense","despesa"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["have","a","cheaper","pair","We"],"ans":"We have a cheaper pair","pt":"Temos um par mais barato."},{"words":["does","this","cost","How","much"],"ans":"How much does this cost","pt":"Quanto custa isto?"}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"mile","pos":"word","pt":"milha","ex":"Run one mile.","expt":"Corra uma milha."},{"w":"quit","pos":"word","pt":"desistir","ex":"Don’t quit.","expt":"Não desista."},{"w":"cost","pos":"word","pt":"custar","ex":"It costs $20.","expt":"Custa 20 dólares."},{"w":"expense","pos":"word","pt":"despesa","ex":"A big expense.","expt":"Uma grande despesa."},{"w":"training plan","pos":"word","pt":"plano de treino","ex":"A training plan.","expt":"Um plano de treino."},{"w":"long run","pos":"word","pt":"corrida longa","ex":"The Sunday long run.","expt":"A corrida longa de domingo."},{"w":"pace","pos":"word","pt":"ritmo","ex":"A steady pace.","expt":"Um ritmo constante."},{"w":"energy gel","pos":"word","pt":"gel de energia","ex":"An energy gel.","expt":"Um gel de energia."},{"w":"blister","pos":"word","pt":"bolha","ex":"A painful blister.","expt":"Uma bolha dolorida."},{"w":"cramp","pos":"word","pt":"cãibra","ex":"A leg cramp.","expt":"Uma cãibra na perna."},{"w":"race bib","pos":"word","pt":"número de corrida","ex":"Pin your race bib.","expt":"Prenda seu número de corrida."},{"w":"starting line","pos":"word","pt":"linha de largada","ex":"The starting line.","expt":"A linha de largada."},{"w":"water station","pos":"word","pt":"posto de água","ex":"A water station.","expt":"Um posto de água."},{"w":"recovery day","pos":"word","pt":"dia de recuperação","ex":"A recovery day.","expt":"Um dia de recuperação."},{"w":"finish medal","pos":"word","pt":"medalha de chegada","ex":"A finish medal.","expt":"Uma medalha de chegada."},{"w":"shin","pos":"word","pt":"canela","ex":"Shin pain.","expt":"Dor na canela."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"culture","t":"Expressões desta aula","body":["**How much does this cost?** — Quanto custa isto?","**It costs two hundred dollars.** — Custa duzentos dólares.","**Wow. I was going to buy it.** — Nossa. Eu ia comprar.","**I’m working on it.** — Estou trabalhando nisso.","**I’m looking for…** — Estou procurando…","**I’m used to it.** — Estou acostumado.","**I’m about to leave.** — Estou prestes a sair."]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"cost","pt":"custar","forms":[["I / you / we / they cost","It costs $20."],["he / she / it costs","This costs a lot."]]}]},{"type":"table","head":["Phrasal verb","Significado","Exemplo"],"rows":[["**give up**","desistir","Don’t give up. — Não desista."]],"cap":"Phrasal verbs"}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Training","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Training","lines":[["Lia","How much does this cost?","Quanto custa isto?"],["Seller","It costs two hundred dollars.","Custa duzentos dólares."],["Lia","Wow. I was going to buy it.","Nossa. Eu ia comprar."],["Seller","We have a cheaper pair.","Temos um par mais barato."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: gonna e wanna (reconhecimento)","items":[{"label":"gonna e wanna (reconhecimento)","note":"Na fala: going to → gonna, want to → wanna. Reconheça; na escrita use a forma completa.","words":["I’m gonna go","I wanna eat","What are you gonna do?"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Say what you were going to do but did not.","pt":"Diga.","model":"I was going to run, but it rained."},{"q":"Ask the price.","pt":"Pergunte.","model":"How much does it cost?"},{"q":"Say what is going to cost a lot.","pt":"Diga.","model":"It is going to cost a lot."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a 6-line story with going to, was going to and cost.","model":"Lia was going to run a marathon. She bought shoes. They cost two hundred dollars. Her mom said, It is going to cost a lot. A friend said, Run with me. It cost nothing.","checklist":["Usei **going to / was going to**","Usei **cost**","6 linhas"],"words":"6 linhas"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “marathon” mean?","opts":["milha","maratona","custar"],"ans":1,"why":"**marathon** = maratona."},{"q":"What does “mile” mean?","opts":["desistir","despesa","milha"],"ans":2,"why":"**mile** = milha."},{"q":"What does “quit” mean?","opts":["desistir","custar","plano de treino"],"ans":0,"why":"**quit** = desistir."},{"q":"What does “cost” mean?","opts":["despesa","custar","linha de chegada"],"ans":1,"why":"**cost** = custar."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Estratégia para as provas","body":["Treine esta habilidade com o formato de tarefas curtas das provas (TOEFL/IELTS).","Leia o enunciado primeiro e procure as palavras-chave."]},{"type":"box","kind":"teach","t":"Nota para o futuro professor","body":["Use exemplos reais da vida dos alunos e peça frases próprias.","Corrija o erro mais frequente da aula em grupo, sem expor o aluno.","Retome o conteúdo na aula seguinte com um exercício curto."]}]}]}